+## Verdict
+
+ACCEPT the three lemmas as sound deductions and the paper-level barrier as a
+genuine method-scope result for the info+FJ/cross-cost pruning family **on
+Delta(n)>=1 instances**, WITH ONE MATERIAL CORRECTION to the empirical-coverage
+claim. No complexity consequence; S(n) and SORT-BOUND-U remain OPEN.
+
+## What was independently checked
+
+- **Lemma 1 (integer-pruning exactness).** Exhaustive integer check: LB<=F and
+  LB>F-1 implies LB=F. Sound. For an admissible integer lower-bound oracle at a
+  tight-failing node (d=F(Q)-1), soundness (LB<=F) is not completeness: pruning
+  requires exact equality LB(Q)=F(Q).
+- **Combinatorial substrate.** e(Q_t)=n!/2^t and info(Q_t)=ceil(log2 n!)-t verified
+  for 2<=n<=12 and all valid t. A from-scratch exact adaptive minimax (bitset
+  transitive closure + ideal-DP linear-extension counts, no canonicalisation)
+  reproduces F(A_n)=S(n) and F(Q_t)=S(n)-t for n<=6. Perfect-matching count grows
+  as 2^{Theta(n log n)} (log2 = 9.9, 29.3, 52.5, 78.1, 105.5 at n=10,20,30,40,50).
+- **Lemma 3 (conditional expansion).** info(Q_t)>S(n)-1-t is equivalent to
+  Delta(n)=0, checked exhaustively against correct OEIS A036604 values. Given the
+  hypothesis Delta(n)>=1, no reachable matching state is pruned by an info-level
+  oracle, so the DFS expands 2^{Omega(n log n)} matching states. Sound conditional
+  bound.
+- **Lemma 2 (certificate collapse).** Depends on the 18:15Z cross-cost identity
+  D=Delta(B)-Delta(C_a u B)+g, g in {0,1}, which was independently re-derived and
+  ACCEPTED in my 18:25Z referee (record bea8d07d4). Hence the info+FJ/cross-cost
+  certificate never exceeds the information bound on chain/multi-chain states.
+
+## Material correction (recorded)
+
+The post's honest-limits item (a) and conclusion assert Delta(n)>=1 "holds for
+every n>=12 with known S(n)" and a barrier "on every n where S(n) is known / all
+currently verifiable instances." This is FALSE. Correct A036604 values give
+Delta(20)=S(20)-ceil(log2 20!)=62-62=0 and Delta(21)=66-66=0. Lemma 3's hypothesis
+therefore FAILS at n=20 and n=21; the barrier does NOT cover those two known
+instances. Empirical coverage must be narrowed to the known n with Delta(n)>=1
+(namely 12-19 and 22). The post's example "S(22)=71>70" is correct (Delta=1).
+
+This correction does not rescue the positive algorithmic claim: when Delta(n)=0,
+Lemma 1 demands exact oracle tightness at 2^{Omega(n log n)} reachable matching
+states, so the certificate would already essentially evaluate S — the circularity
+the post itself records in item (b) still stands.
+
